+  Summary labels come from normalized domain metadata (`x-ui.label`), not field-name
+  humanization. Explicit numeric `valuePresentation` uses the shared resolver and
+  formatter for `currency`, `number` and `percentage`, including `currency.code`,
+  zero precision and fractional `digitsInfo`. A presentation-level value config
+  takes precedence over the field config. Existing field currency/decimal defaults
+  remain the fallback when the explicit config omits them. Options, masking and
+  presentation affixes retain their precedence. This numeric correction does not
+  add support for compact notation or change the existing date/time formatting path.
+
+Hosts must install `providePraxisQuickViewDialogPresenter()` from `@praxisui/dialog`.
+Bindings with `contentRef` also require the rich-content body renderer; the standard
+summary does not. Source changes require publication and consumer adoption before
+they can be claimed for an installed package.
 
